     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Is there any similar function like unload or unattach got called when I exit shiny apps?<div><br></div><div>The thing is this: A colleague of mine created a Shiny app, which can connect to the database and do some work. However, after he presses Ctrl+c to exit Shiny, he wants to automatically call the database disconnect function to stop the connection. Otherwise, the connection is still there and not closed.</div><div><br></div><div>Is there any way to do that?</div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
